The mechanism is narrow and transcript-bound: $\text{listen to authority}
\longrightarrow
\text{humble yourself}
\longrightarrow
\text{stand under authority}
\longrightarrow
\text{carry authority}.$ That sequence keeps the lecture from becoming generic advice to be humble. The sharper point is that humility is a condition for being corrected, and being corrected is part of becoming credible enough to lead.

